                        # etc.) for input. If this global is false, then an older style abbreviation is also allowed (e.g. M1 for the first routing layer, M2 for the second routing layer, etc.).This layer
                        # abbreviation style is not recommended, and is only allowed for backward compatibility to migrate older scripts.  Eventually this global will be removed, so you should modify your
                        # scripts to use LEF/OA layer names, or routing-layer index values for -layer options to avoid problems in the future.
